  "ArticleContents": "🔧 Poly Beats: Eclipse 0.10.2\nMore bug fixes, tending toward the themes side and some stuff relating to judgement and gameplay. Let's get it!\n\nChanges\n- You can now skip the fail animation via \"Skip Fail Animation\" in Game settings. (Crafty)\n- Moved \"Audio Sync Offset\" setting over to the Audio menu.\n- You can now use Themes you haven't uploaded to the Steam Workshop. (Crafty)\n- \"Develop Themes\" has been renamed to \"Local Themes\" for easier finding. (Crafty)\n- You can now set your local Themes inside the main Theme selector panel if you don't feel like messing with yours at that moment. (Crafty)\n- If a map doesn't have note jump speed set, and it hasn't been set in map files - it will default to 12 unless you override it.\n\nBugs Fixed\n- Fixed resolutions sometimes not applying once you set them. (Crafty)\n- Fixed v-sync being enabled when not in fullscreen. (Crafty)\n- Fixed fullscreen sometimes not applying, and not persisting between sessions. (Crafty)\n- Fixed a bug where hold notes don't affect your accuracy. Again. How does this keep happening? (Crafty)\n- Fixed a bug where hold notes double-incremented the combo count (Crafty)\n- Fixed an issue on Galactic Warfare and PRIMAL RAGE where scores on those maps would not submit - yes, it was about spaces. (Crafty)\n- Fixed a bug where it takes you to miss at least 2 notes for a combo streak to break. (Crafty)\n- Fixed a bug where Atychiphobia charts just didn't work.\n- Fixed a bug where hold note SFX can be heard before they spawn.\n\n**Known Bugs**\n- There's an issue with ANNIHILATION and the right side of tracks. Bare with.\n\nGOOD PAN",
